- Not backed by the material: no actual CycleNet repo (L appears in the paper/code as the "cycle" hyperparameter of data-induced cyclic projection; the repo is absent so no code-level details can be verified); no datasets (the task environment's dataset list is empty) — the standard benchmarks (ETTm1/m2, Weather, Traffic, Electricity, Sales) are from the paper but not present here; no compute resources — number of seeds / grid size is a placeholder (3 seeds; L-grid design ~8–10 values per dataset) and must be validated against the researcher's actual compute resources; no GPU; no scientific Python stack and no network → even the design-support computations (plotting ACF) cannot be executed here without a researcher-provided environment or offline wheels.
- Uncertainties: whether CycleNet's official protocol uses a single L per dataset or per channel; handling of multivariate series where channels have different cycles (propose per-dataset majority vote / weighted average, needs confirmation); the handling of a 168 weekly peak in Traffic.

