## 3. Phase B — ACF Estimator (Deterministic Pseudocode)
Formal pseudocode:

```
function select_L_acf(y_train, params):
  1. y ← instance-normalize(y_train) (zero mean, unit std) [scale invariance; for the differencing step]
  2. d ← 1 if ADF-like trend heuristic? No — deterministically: always apply first-difference if raw ACF at lag 1 > 0.9? Must be deterministic.
```

Deterministic detrending rule needed. Proposal: use differenced series for the ACF only when ACF_raw(τ) > 0.8 for all τ ∈ 1..4 (sign of strong trend / persistence); otherwise raw series. Actually, simpler and more deterministic: always compute ACF on both raw and first-difference, and select based on the protocol below; but that doubles the branches. Better: fix a single policy — apply seasonal-neutral policy: "if ACF_raw does not fall below 0.5 by τ_max/2, compute ACF on once-differenced series" — deterministic and simple. Formalize with explicit constants.

Full pseudocode:

```
PARAMS (fixed): τ_min=4; z=3; harmonic support threshold factor h=0.6; max lag τ_max=min(floor(N/4), 336); FFT for cross-check; K=3 shortlist size.

function PEAK_SELECT(ρ, n, params):
  1. θ(τ) = z * sqrt((1 + 2 * Σ_{j=1}^{τ-1} ρ(j)²) / n)   # Bartlett-adjusted SE, per-lag
  2. P = {τ ∈ [τ_min, τ_max] : ρ(τ) > θ(τ) and τ is local max: ρ(τ)>ρ(τ±1)}
  3. if P == ∅: return FALLBACK_FFT(y)          # see 6
  4. For each τ ∈ P sorted ascending: support S(τ) = |{k ∈ {2,3} : ρ(kτ) > h·θ(kτ)}|
     (guard kτ ≤ τ_max; skip out-of-range)
  5. P' = {τ ∈ P : S(τ) ≥ 1}   # eligible = at least one harmonic
  6. if P' ≠ ∅: L_acf = min(P')  # smallest τ with harmonic support
     else: L_acf = argmax_{τ∈P} ρ(τ)   # fallback: global peak among eligible peaks
  7. Tiebreak: if multiple τ within the same candidate have |ρ diff| < 0.02 → smallest τ.
  8. Shortlist: L1 = L_acf; L2, L3 = next local peaks by ρ among P \ {multiples/submultiples of L1}; include FFT top if discrepancy.
  9. FFT cross-check: f* = argmax periodogram over frequency band [1/τ_max, 1/τ_min] (after Hann window, detrended series); τ_fft = round(N_f / f*)...
     if |τ_fft − L1| > 1 and ρ-based peaks don't match either → append τ_fft to shortlist.
```

Fallback when no peaks: first FFT (also deterministic); if FFT dominant period has spectral concentration below threshold (e.g., peak power < 3× median band power → "no cycle evidence"), default to L=1 (cycle-less ablation arm) and flag the dataset as non-periodic for analysis. This is the explicit no-peak rule: FFT first, L=1 as terminal fallback.

